       </property>
      </widget>
     </item>
     <item>
      <widget class="QLabel" name="about_bands_label">
       <property name="text">
        <string>&lt;b&gt;Frequency bands&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;• Add a new band with "Add", or load an existing file with "Load". You can edit the bands loaded.&lt;br/&gt;• Double-click a cell to edit its value. The values must be within the frequency bins available, so add the reports in step 1, "Input Files", first.&lt;br/&gt;• "Remove" removes the selected band. "Save" saves the bands you edited in a .tsv file, which "Load" can read later.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;b&gt;Absolute and relative power&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;• The spectral power can be absolute or relative.&lt;br/&gt;• For absolute power, fill only the numerator of the band, "num-start(Hz)" and "num-end(Hz)". Leave "den-start(Hz)" and "den-end(Hz)" as nan (not a number).&lt;br/&gt;• For relative power, fill the numerator and the denominator of the band. The relative power is the power of the numerator band divided by the power of the denominator band, in percent.&lt;br/&gt;• For example, 1 to 4 Hz over 0.5 to 32 Hz gives the power from 1 to 4 Hz as a percentage of the power from 0.5 to 32 Hz.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;b&gt;Frequency bins&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;• A band includes its low frequency bin and excludes its high one, [low, high[. So the power of a frequency bin is never averaged twice in two adjacent bands.&lt;br/&gt;• For example, with bins of 0.5 Hz, the band 1 to 4 Hz holds the 6 bins that start at 1, 1.5, 2, 2.5, 3 and 3.5 Hz. The band 4 to 8 Hz starts with the bin at 4 Hz.&lt;br/&gt;• Use band limits that are limits of the frequency bins. A band whose bins are not all in a report is left empty for that channel.</string>
       </property>
       <property name="textFormat">
        <enum>Qt::TextFormat::RichText</enum>
       </property>
       <property name="wordWrap">
        <bool>true</bool>
       </property>
       <property name="variant" stdset="0">
        <string notr="true">help</string>
       </property>
      </widget>
     </item>
    </layout>
   </item>
  </layout>
